   "subject": "Announcing packrat 0.2.0",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div></div><div><h1 style=\"margin:1.3em 0px 1em;padding:0px;font-weight:bold;font-size:1.6em;border-bottom-width:1px;border-bottom-style:solid;border-bottom-color:rgb(221,221,221)\">Packrat 0.2.0</h1>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">We’re excited to announce version 0.2.0 of packrat! We’ve introduced a number<br>of exciting features in this release:</p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\"><strong><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat_mode</code></strong> allows you to seamlessly step in and out of packrat mode,<br>for when you would would like to manage or use external projects while<br>working with a packrat project. In addition, once you have entered packrat<br>mode, the project directory is remembered for all later calls to packrat<br>functions, e.g. <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">snapshot</code>, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">clean</code>, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">restore</code>, and so on — so calling these<br>functions without arguments will use the project directory, even if you have<br>navigated outside of the project or to a project sub-directory.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">The packrat project files have been migrated into a single <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat/</code> folder<br>— this keeps pollution in the base directory of your project down. The<br>remappings are:</p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em;margin:0px;padding-left:1em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat.sources</code> -&gt; <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat/src</code>,</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">library</code> -&gt; <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat/lib</code>,</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat.lock</code> -&gt; <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat/packrat.lock</code>, and</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">.Renviron</code> file has been removed.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\"><strong><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">bundle</code></strong> and <strong><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">unbundle</code></strong> allow you to zip up your project as a tarball<br>for easy sharing,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\"><strong><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">with_extlib</code></strong> and <strong><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">extlib</code></strong> allow you to (temporarily) load and use<br>packages within the user library; this can be useful if you want to leverage<br>another package (for example, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">devtools::install_github</code>) while avoiding<br>dependencies on <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">devtools</code> itself,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Packrat can now handle source package tarballs, rather than just source<br>package folders,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">A number of bugs relating to <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">status()</code> output have been fixed and tweaked,<br>to give better information to the user.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Projects in packrat mode will have automatic, asynchronous snapshots for safe<br>actions: with automatic snapshots on, packrat will automatically upgrade<br>packages that are out of date, or add packages that are new to the lock file<br>(e.g. when seen by an <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">install.packages()</code> call). Downgrades, removals and<br>‘crossgrades’ will be ignored and will require you to take an appropriate<br>action (guided by the information provided by <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">status()</code>).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Packrat will warn you if you have user libraries in the system library path.<br>In addition, packrat supplies a script for OS X users, to assist in migrating<br>user packages from the system library to a separate user library. (By<br>default, R versions compiled for Mac OS X install all packages into the<br>system library; for packrat to function correctly we require that user and<br>system libraries be separate — this script should help facilitate the<br>process. If you have any problems with migration, please let us know!)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">We will also be working on integration with the RStudio IDE in the coming<br>weeks: here, we can provide a user-friendly interface for many of the packrat<br>actions, and also leverage many tools within the IDE for better and smarter<br>automatic updating of your packrat projects. Stay tuned!</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">If you’d like to migrate a ‘packrat 0.1.0’ project to the new format, please do<br>the following:</p>\r\n<ol style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">Navigate to your packrat project directory,</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">Remove the project <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">.Rprofile</code> file,</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">Start an R session in this folder,</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Run the following script:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> if (!require(&quot;devtools&quot;)) install.packages(&quot;devtools&quot;)<br> devtools::install_github(&quot;rstudio/packrat&quot;)<br> packrat::migrate()</font></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">After this, you can restart your R session, and you should be good to go!</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Thanks,<br>Kevin</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj4jIFBhY2tyYXQgMC4yLjA8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PldlJ3JlIGV4Y2l0\r\nZWQgdG8gYW5ub3VuY2UgdmVyc2lvbiAwLjIuMCBvZiBwYWNrcmF0ISBXZSd2ZSBpbnRyb2R1Y2Vk\r\nIGEgbnVtYmVyPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5vZiBleGNpdGluZyBmZWF0dXJlcyBpbiB0aGlzIHJlbGVhc2U6\r\nPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4tICoqYHBhY2tyYXRfbW9kZWAqKiBhbGxvd3MgeW91\r\nIHRvIHNlYW1sZXNzbHkgc3RlcCBpbiBhbmQgb3V0IG9mIHBhY2tyYXQgbW9kZSw8L2Rpdj48ZGl2\r\nPiZuYnNwOyBmb3Igd2hlbiB5b3Ugd291bGQgd291bGQgbGlrZSB0byBtYW5hZ2Ugb3IgdXNlIGV4\r\ndGVybmFsIHByb2plY3RzIHdoaWxlPC9kaXY+PGRpdj4mbmJzcDsgd29ya2luZyB3aXRoIGEgcGFj\r\na3JhdCBwcm9qZWN0LiBJbiBhZGRpdGlvbiwgb25jZSB5b3UgaGF2ZSBlbnRlcmVkIHBhY2tyYXQ8\r\nL2Rpdj48ZGl2PiZuYnNwOyBtb2RlLCB0aGUgcHJvamVjdCBkaXJlY3RvcnkgaXMgcmVtZW1iZXJl\r\nZCBmb3IgYWxsIGxhdGVyIGNhbGxzIHRvIHBhY2tyYXQ8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiZuYnNwOyBmdW5jdGlv\r\nbnMsIGUuZy4gYHNuYXBzaG90YCwgYGNsZWFuYCwgYHJlc3RvcmVgLCBhbmQgc28gb24gLS0gc28g\r\nY2FsbGluZyB0aGVzZTwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm